attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a short spine.** Columns 0 to 1, `lipA` to `tatE`, are carried by 94 to 100% of chromosomes, all persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0% of calls {S1, P}. The model names 99 to 99.8% of them, fewest at column 0, `lipA`, 99% {S1}.

@variable **A single variable column follows**, column 2, `ybeM`, carried by 78% {S2.c2}. Then columns 3 to 17, `crcB` to `rnk`, are [[citrate lyase]] at columns 9 to 15, carried by 90 to 94% {S3, Q}. Through columns 61 to 63 a branch of 3 shell families runs in 16 to 35%, and through columns 73 to 77 a branch of 5 shell families runs in 11 to 13% {S16.b61, S16.b73}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 97 against 84%, and hesitates less there, 0.19 against 0.80 bits {M}. It hesitates most at column 63, `fimZ`, a fork column, 1.85 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends in fork and variable columns.** Columns 61 to 79 are carried by 21 to 85% of chromosomes, in a region of plasticity in 44 to 93% of calls {S16, P}. The last column is `ylbE`, in 21% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 92% of genes**, 0.40 bits on average, perplexity 1.4 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 1.19 against 0.20 bits, and names fewer genes, 78% against 96% {C}.

